WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Carv3D: from a block to a print-ready part – directly on the model, no feature tree

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:14.100
Click a face and sketch: a circle on the top face

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.800
Pull: the circle becomes a post, and you type the height as a number

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.700
Click an edge, choose "Chamfer": a 10 mm bevel

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:36.500
Add a fillet of 5 mm

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:47.700
Holes work on slanted faces too: the screw stands square to the face

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:54.400
Colour a face: the colour goes into the 3MF export

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:04.000
"Offset edge": a line 10 mm from the edge splits the face

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.700
Press the new strip in by 2 mm

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:20.700
"Split face": two clicks set the dividing line

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.200
Pull the split face: a rib appears

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:34.400
Click a round face and drag the arrow: the radius changes

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:41.300
Generator "Box with lid": check the sizes, one click

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:46.200
Box and lid lie on the bed, ready to print

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.300
Export as 3MF: with colours, straight to your slicer

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:57.000
Carv3D – local 3D modelling for 3D printing and makers · carv3d.de
